1
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,180
Try stepping away and take a look.

2
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:28,860
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:35,560
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:42,720
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:47,960
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:53,780
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:59,920
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:02,040
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:09,360
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:14,920
Go on, turn that corner.

11
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:20,140
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:28,060
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari!

13
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:33,260
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:34,880
Thank you.

15
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,300
Yay!

16
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,620
Yay!

17
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,120
Darn it!

18
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,340
The winner is Mr. Sanedera
from Katsushika Ward.

19
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:11,920
Cheers!

20
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:18,380
Our one-two finish again this year

21
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:23,940
But it's only 5,000 yen.
Until last year, it was 30,000, wasn't it?

22
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:27,560
Come to think of it, the trophy
also seems to have gotten smaller.

23
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:30,860
Ryotsu, that guy...

24
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:33,700
N-no way...

25
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,940
Don't do anything rash!

26
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:38,340
What?

27
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:41,380
If you stay alive,
good things are sure to happen, right?

28
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:42,240
Let me go.

29
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,480
I'm going.

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,120
Sakonji

31
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,640
Ryotsu

32
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,480
Alright, you're okay.

33
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,300
Slowly get up and reach out your hand.

34
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:57,709
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

35
00:02:57,759 --> 00:03:01,485
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

36
00:03:01,535 --> 00:03:05,236
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

37
00:03:05,286 --> 00:03:09,038
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

38
00:03:09,088 --> 00:03:12,777
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

39
00:03:12,827 --> 00:03:16,566
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

40
00:03:16,616 --> 00:03:20,331
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

41
00:03:20,381 --> 00:03:24,280
I, I, I, I, I, I, I, I,
I, I, I, I, I, I, I...

42
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:30,620
You were trying to stop me. Come to my restaurant tomorrow.
I'll let you eat as many tacos as you want.

43
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,800
Tacos

44
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,880
I'm tacos, Mexican cuisine!

45
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:48,800
This is pretty good. It's my first time eating one, but it's quite tasty.
So this is what gets delivered?

46
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,860
Yes, my name is Señor Taco.

47
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:54,980
Ever since I was a child,
tacos have been my favorite food.

48
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:58,560
But in Japan, tacos aren't very well known.

49
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:01,520
Even when you order tacos at an izakaya,

50
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,160
what they end up bringing
out is a birdhouse.

51
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:06,000
When I was at home, I made them myself,

52
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,420
but when business trips or overtime went on and on,
that wasn't possible either.

53
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:11,660
That's when I thought,

54
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:14,500
pizza wasn't a major
dish in the past either.

55
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,240
But with the spread of pizza delivery,

56
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,640
now there's no one who doesn't know it.

57
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:22,120
That's it,
why don't tacos start delivering too?

58
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:26,320
So I quit my salaried job
and decided to open this shop.

59
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:27,140
I see.

60
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:30,440
Our meeting here must be fate.

61
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:33,640
You said the tacos were delicious earlier,
didn't you?

62
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:37,920
Actually, we're looking for a delivery person
who looks like they have plenty of stamina.

63
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:39,460
You've got to be kidding.

64
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:41,100
We're not that free, either.

65
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:42,880
Let's go home, Sagonji.

66
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,440
Yeah.

67
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,300
Wait up.

68
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,120
How about 10,000 yen an hour?

69
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,400
10,000 yen an hour.

70
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:53,160
100,000 yen for 10 hours a day.

71
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,660
1,000,000 yen in 10 days.

72
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:56,600
3,000,000 yen in one month.

73
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,980
Your spirit in devoting
yourself to spreading tacos

74
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,080
That's truly admirable.

75
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:06,320
Though I'm not much, I, Kankichi Ryotsu,

76
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,140
will lend you a hand.

77
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:09,960
Thank you. Will you do it, then?

78
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:12,180
Well then, let's get started.

79
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:15,120
Let's quickly open Amigo!

80
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:15,780
Amigo!

81
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:19,740
Come on, delivery tacos, mucho!

82
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,680
We open today!

83
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:23,020
Tacos

84
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:24,820
I'll try taking this route this time.

85
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:32,840
Actually,
this location has a major drawback.

86
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:35,680
It has a great view. Isn't it a good spot?

87
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,940
You'll understand once you
actually make deliveries.

88
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,000
Yes, this is Taco Mono
Nam Mucho home delivery.

89
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,580
If it's here, yes, yes, that's fine.

90
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:46,040
We're going.

91
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,260
Taco Sancho.

92
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:49,540
Yes.

93
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:50,840
Here it is.

94
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:53,640
From here it won't take even five minutes.

95
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:54,820
Got it, I'm counting on you.

96
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:55,420
It's ready.

97
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:56,000
Alright.

98
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,160
We're short on time, you know.

99
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:14,960
It's only gone four floors so far!

100
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,700
What is this elevator?

101
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:23,720
It only moves one floor at a time!

102
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:27,780
I'm getting off! Let me out!

103
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,720
Damn it, the stairs are faster.

104
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:43,200
It took a full 30 minutes to get down.

105
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:45,140
If we don't hurry,
the client's going to be furious!

106
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,540
I'm back.

107
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:57,000
You're late! The customer has called
again and again to chase the order!

108
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,260
I know, it takes way too long
to get down to the first floor.

109
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:05,040
That's why I told you,
that's this shop's biggest flaw.

110
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,640
It's too big. It's almost fatal!

111
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:10,000
Why did you open a shop
in a place like this?

112
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:11,700
Well, just take a look.

113
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,200
What?

114
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,520
It's the lease agreement for this shop.

115
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:19,300
I rented this place thinking it was B1,
meaning the first basement level.

116
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,480
First basement level?

117
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:20,760
Yeah.

118
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:23,140
Where's the first basement level here?

119
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:26,460
Look at where the papers say B1.

120
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:30,980
Here it is. The part that says B1.

121
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,322
But this isn't a B, it's a 6,

122
00:07:33,372 --> 00:07:35,960
meaning it's the 61st floor.

123
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:38,600
Looking closely, it really is a 6.

124
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,800
You didn't notice right away?

125
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:44,720
After just finishing the contract,
I left the shop construction to others

126
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:48,640
and went off to Mexico,
the home of tacos, to train.

127
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:49,960
But then...

128
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,240
W-what is this...

129
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:56,560
So the construction was already finished
when he came back to the country?

130
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:59,540
Yes, the problem is the
distance down to ground level.

131
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:03,660
If we could ride a bike
straight down to the ground,

132
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:04,820
by the stairs?

133
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,760
That's impossible.

134
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:09,920
No, there's one person who can do it.

135
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:11,170
Well then,

136
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:15,000
Taco Cosmo Namucho delivery,
express by high-speed motorcycle!

137
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:17,320
Senpai, what is this?

138
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,960
Why am I wearing this outfit?

139
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,140
Is he going to be all right? This guy,

140
00:08:23,190 --> 00:08:26,280
doesn't really look like
he can ride a motorcycle.

141
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,380
Well, let's just watch him.

142
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:32,469
Yes, this is Mo' Nachos Taco Delivery.

143
00:08:32,519 --> 00:08:34,460
Yes, yes, we'll deliver it right away.

144
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,260
Taco Nicchan.

145
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:36,880
Yes.

146
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:38,540
Honda, it's your turn.

147
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,360
I'm the one delivering it?

148
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,320
That's why I brought you here, isn't it?

149
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,680
Come on.

150
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:45,340
Done!

151
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,760
Alright, hurry up, Honda!

152
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,600
B-but...

153
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,320
Sorry,

154
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,075
With me,

155
00:08:51,125 --> 00:08:55,640
Deliver it from up there.

156
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:56,920
Right, I'm counting on you!

157
00:08:59,820 --> 00:09:02,260
Amigo, that's an incredible speed.

158
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:04,460
I told you it'd be fine, didn't I?

159
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,920
But the stairs...

160
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,500
He'll be fine, don't worry.

161
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,800
He's already back?

162
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,320
I delivered it.

163
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,480
All right, good job.

164
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,180
That's an incredible speed.

165
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,720
Senpai, the stairs were a real struggle.

166
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:34,320
Here are your tacos.

167
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:36,380
The tacos...

168
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:40,300
We'll make sure this never happens again.

169
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,780
I'm terribly sorry.

170
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:42,660
Yeah, yeah.

171
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:45,140
Of course, we'll refund the cost.

172
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:45,600
Yes.

173
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:47,880
What happened?

174
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:50,960
The tacos from earlier
had their fillings spill out

175
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,500
and got completely squashed, apparently.

176
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:53,260
Well...

177
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:58,520
Well, with that much impact, it's no wonder.

178
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,060
What a blunder.

179
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:02,840
It's because you didn't drive
more carefully and slowly.

180
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,020
You're the one who told me to hurry, senpai!

181
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,760
Hurry, but carry it carefully!

182
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:08,440
Please don't tell them it was me.

183
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,760
No motorcycles.

184
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,900
Isn't there another way to
get it all the way down at once?

185
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:14,580
All the way down at once

186
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:17,000
Yes, that's it!

187
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:21,460
Here you go! Our premium Tacos Mucho,
delivered free of charge!

188
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:28,680
Why do I always end up getting
dragged into these things?

189
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:31,940
This is the surest and fastest way,
so there.

190
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:33,380
How about the Volvo?

191
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:34,260
Okay!

192
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:35,160
An order just came in.

193
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:37,400
Deliver it right away.

194
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,140
Alright, here goes!

195
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:41,760
The destination is
pasted on top of this box.

196
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:43,400
Since the motorcycle is parked downstairs,

197
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:45,180
ride this down all the way to the bottom.

198
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:46,420
No, no.

199
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:48,140
N-no way, that's impossible!

200
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:49,720
Shut up and stop complaining!

201
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,540
It's a gondola that Volvo improved.

202
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:52,500
Don't worry.

203
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:53,800
"Don't worry," he says...

204
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,500
Volvo, do it!

205
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:57,300
Okay!

206
00:10:58,180 --> 00:10:58,820
Whoa -

207
00:10:58,820 --> 00:10:59,900
Worried?

208
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:01,460
Don't worry.

209
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:03,480
That belt's holding you in tight.

210
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:05,020
Even if something happens, you won't die.

211
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:23,500


212
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:23,900
Bungee!

213
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,060
Bungee jumping?

214
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,820
Bro, this way you can get all the
way down to the ground in one go!

215
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:31,640
It's about ten seconds to the bottom.

216
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:33,920
Japan's biggest free fall

217
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:42,340
It stopped.

218
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:43,440
As expected, he's fast.

219
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,160
What happened?

220
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:46,140
Honda isn't moving at all!

221
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:48,460
Don't tell me he crashed into the ground?

222
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,640
No, he should've stopped just in time.

223
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:52,340
Honda!

224
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:55,400
He's just knocked out.

225
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:57,960
Come on, wake up! Hurry and carry him!

226
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:03,500
Calm down, Honda. It's over now.

227
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:04,320
Honda

228
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:07,700
Senpai, am I still alive?

229
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:11,520
Of course you are. Passing out over that little thing,
how pathetic.

230
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:16,420
Thank goodness. I had a dream
I grew wings and went to heaven.

231
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,360
I want real wings too.

232
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:23,700
If we had those, we could just fly
out the window and make the delivery.

233
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:26,460
Wait.

234
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:29,420
Maybe we could actually do it.

235
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:31,700
Yeah, we can do it.

236
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:33,800
We fly through the sky.

237
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:35,280
Fly through the sky?

238
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:37,680
Yes, the flying taco-high-bin!

239
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,780
W-what is this thing?

240
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:52,600
It's a portable hang glider
we're developing in-house.

241
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:55,400
Wear this and you'll be
able to fly through the sky.

242
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,260
Fly through the sky?

243
00:12:56,620 --> 00:12:58,120
Everything's ready on this end.

244
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,840
Good, test run, Nakagawa.

245
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:00,440
Yes.

246
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,360
Please, just stop.

247
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,480
It'll be fine.

248
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:05,840
Trust in the technology
of the Nakagawa Group.

249
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:13,060
Stand at the tip of that board, and then...

250
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:15,060
No good, he's passed out...

251
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:17,340
Can't be helped. I'll do it myself.

252
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:20,500
Looks like you've become
a true hero of justice.

253
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:21,640
Leave it to you.

254
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,960
Leave it to me!

255
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,920
Spread your arms out to the sides!
Like a flying squirrel!

256
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:32,700
Got it!

257
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:36,040
Yahoo!

258
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,400
Hup!

259
00:13:37,540 --> 00:13:38,260
It worked!

260
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:40,800
Nihoho!

261
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:48,880
Hey, aren't you slacking off?

262
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:51,480
Ryotsu, how on earth did you

263
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:54,680
We've found a new way to deliver!

264
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:57,840
Now, taco delivery, Mona Mucho!

265
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,800
We're delivering from the sky, no less!

266
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,920
Here comes the flying delivery service!

267
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,840
A flying delivery service, really?

268
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:08,020
Yes, this is Flying
Delivery Taco's Mona Mucho.

269
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:14,760
It's Honda. Count on me, senpai. And it's
been upgraded even further, with a helmet.

270
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:17,820
I've installed the navigation device.
Please lower your hood.

271
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:25,340
This is it. The red dot is blinking.
Keep that red dot centered in your hood.

272
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:28,100
If you fly in that direction,
you'll reach the destination.

273
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,220
There it is.

274
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:33,940
Here I go.

275
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,960
Senpai,
you've really made that suit your own.

276
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:39,960
He's a man of real power.

277
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,760
That's his only redeeming quality,
after all.

278
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:43,640
Yeah, that's right.

279
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:48,160
That's the building.

280
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:53,100
Your tacos have arrived.

281
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,320
Already here?
It hasn't even been three minutes!

282
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,420
Flying taco delivery
really is something else.

283
00:14:57,420 --> 00:15:00,860
Your tacos have arrived.

284
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:01,640
Thank you for your hard work.

285
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,580
Your tacos have arrived.

286
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:05,460
Thanks for your trouble.

287
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:08,100
Your tacos have arrived.

288
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,220
Sakyu!

289
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:10,880
Yes, this is Monamuncho.

290
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:12,360
Yes, this is Monamuncho from Taco Aibin.

291
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:12,840
Yes.

292
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:13,940
Yes, understood.

293
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:15,120
I'm back.

294
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:18,140
Senpai, sorry, please come out right away.

295
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:20,180
Hey, let me go to the bathroom.

296
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:23,360
Sorry, orders are pouring in.

297
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:24,620
Please hold on.

298
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:25,040
What?

299
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,680
Porma, please lower it a little.

300
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:31,380
Hey, hey,
Nakagawa can't possibly do this alone.

301
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:33,060
You two, help him out too.

302
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:34,680
Understood.

303
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,260
Alright, okay, please go ahead.

304
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:38,420
Well...

305
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,580
Do I have to do it too?

306
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,240
Of course you do.

307
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:45,060
I made Honda's one extra special, you know.

308
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:47,480
Honda, hold that handle and give it a try.

309
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,860
The handle?

310
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:52,020
Just say the word, mister,
and I'll take you anywhere!

311
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:53,440
That's it, keep it up.

312
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,260
There's no describing the thrill
of slicing through the wind!

313
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:04,120
This is the best!

314
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,920
Hey, Kinji!

315
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:10,580
Keep your hands steady
and grab hold of the wind.

316
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:13,880
Good luck!

317
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:17,520
I've got hang gliding experience, you know.

318
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:19,020
Easy, easy!

319
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,000
No way!

320
00:16:25,060 --> 00:16:26,280
What are you doing?

321
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:29,040
Senpai, I'm going this way then.

322
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:29,860
Count on you!

323
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,080
Gracias, amigos!

324
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:44,240
Thanks to you all,
our Mucho tacos are the talk of the town.

325
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:47,320
And today, a big order has finally come in.

326
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:52,540
They want tacos delivered to this big Mexican restaurant
next week.

327
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:56,677
If this succeeds,
tacos will spread across all of Japan,

328
00:16:56,727 --> 00:16:59,840
no, across the entire world.

329
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:02,560
But if we fail,
it could become an international incident.

330
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,540
We absolutely cannot afford to fail.

331
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:07,660
So if we succeed, I'll double your pay.

332
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:08,220
Yay!

333
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:10,760
Put your heart into the work.

334
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:11,140
Yes.

335
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:12,040
Yes.

336
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:21,060
Shall we send them out to deliver?

337
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,220
Honda, pull yourself together, Honda!

338
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
What happened? Who did this to you?

339
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:39,280
The other guy was a flying delivery man too.

340
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:39,900
What?

341
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:42,060
Could it be...

342
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:42,960
This is bad, Ryotsu!

343
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:45,020
Look outside the window.

344
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,420
A flying takoyaki delivery?

345
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,540
Takoyaki... I knew it.

346
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:55,780
Delivery for Mr. Monamucho!

347
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,000
Yes.

348
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:05,540
Long time no see, big brother.

349
00:18:05,540 --> 00:18:06,040
Yakio.

350
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:07,620
You look just alike.

351
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:08,480
So you're brothers.

352
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:10,160
Takota Yakio.

353
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:12,520
He's my twin younger brother.

354
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:15,740
Looks like you've been getting
quite the talk around town.

355
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:18,380
But don't get too cocky.
This is where it ends.

356
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:21,740
I'll humiliate you at the
big Mexico Expo next week.

357
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:22,800
What did you say?

358
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,680
This is the price for
betraying the Takota clan.

359
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:29,940
What a strange guy.

360
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:32,320
So the day has finally come.

361
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,780
The Takota clan, the takoyaki shop owners,

362
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:38,340
my ancestor was a man named Hachibei Takota.

363
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:41,740
This man was a huge takoyaki lover.

364
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:46,120
But back then, takoyaki was
still not very well known in Japan.

365
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:50,640
As Hachibei lay dying, he left a will

366
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:54,180
saying,
"You can eat takoyaki anytime, anywhere!"

367
00:18:55,680 --> 00:19:02,240
Let me say, from that day on, spreading
takoyaki became the mission of the Takota clan.

368
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:15,440
Through their efforts, takoyaki became a food known across the nation.
Hachibei's will was finally fulfilled. So this time, I'm going to focus on my own favorite food.

369
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:21,660
I've decided to stake my life on spreading tacos.
But it seems my brother doesn't see it that way.

370
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:25,900
He said he'd make you look like a fool at the Big Mexico shop,
didn't he?

371
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:28,460
He's planning to sabotage the deliveries,
isn't he?

372
00:19:28,460 --> 00:19:31,520
But I have a long-held wish to spread tacos.

373
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:33,620
I can't give in to his sabotage.

374
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:36,680
Ryotsu,
I'm leaving the delivery on the day to you.

375
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:39,960
If it succeeds,
I'll pay you a special bonus.

376
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:41,340
Alright, leave it to me.

377
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:44,480
Yes, yes, understood. Thank you very much.

378
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,700
It's here!
An order from the Big Mexico shop!

379
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:49,900
Alright, it's ready!

380
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:53,180
That's amazing.

381
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:58,320
Senpai, this is the rocket booster our
company newly developed for aircraft use.

382
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:02,840
If the time comes, use this to
fly straight to the exhibition hall.

383
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:03,740
Got it.

384
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:08,500
But this has too much power, so whatever
you do, don't set it to maximum power.

385
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,240
Understood.

386
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:16,200
If this succeeds, we'll be getting a huge
number of orders during the Big Mexico Fair.

387
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,780
Good luck, Ryotsu.

388
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:18,720
Fight!

389
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:21,380
Senpai, please come back safely.

390
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:23,120
Count on me, Honda.

391
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:24,840
Leave it to me!

392
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:40,000
I knew they wouldn't
let us through so easily.

393
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,600
I'll crush your brother's shop!

394
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:43,800
Help!

395
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:47,620
It's him!

396
00:20:48,420 --> 00:20:50,140
Wh-what?!

397
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:54,900
How about that?

398
00:20:58,420 --> 00:20:59,360
This is the end.

399
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:01,200
Ryo-san!

400
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,320
I've come to help you!

401
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:05,220
Everyone!

402
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:07,600
What kind of

403
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:09,400
mask do you think I came wearing?

404
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,960
Leave this to us.

405
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:11,700
Got it.

406
00:21:12,900 --> 00:21:13,560
Brother.

407
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,900
Why won't you understand baseball?

408
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:18,240
Surely spreading takoyaki is enough already.

409
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:19,640
If it's a takoyaki mission,

410
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:22,740
it's only natural to devote
your life to spreading takoyaki.

411
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:24,940
Even after saying this much,
you still don't get it?

412
00:21:24,940 --> 00:21:26,100
I don't.

413
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:31,560
Damn, this is

414
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:34,680
Yes!

415
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:37,720
a turbulence zone between the buildings!

416
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:39,260
What's that supposed to mean?

417
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:45,420
The wind between the factory buildings is
tangling together and creating turbulence.

418
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:46,960
You set me up, Yakio!

419
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:49,820
You meant to drive us
into this from the start.

420
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:53,660
May this turbulence blow your
brother's ambitions away, too.

421
00:21:55,740 --> 00:21:57,560
Senpai, we're running out of time!

422
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:02,000
Full power on the Yam-Wen booster,
and we fly straight to the venue!

423
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,220
That's too dangerous!

424
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:06,560
There's no other way to
cut through this turbulence.

425
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:08,920
Senpai!

426
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:14,940
Here I go!

427
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:16,120
Damn it!

428
00:22:16,740 --> 00:22:17,620
Screw it!

429
00:22:23,220 --> 00:22:23,800
There it is!

430
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:30,460
Ambassador, business is booming.
Congratulations.

431
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:32,860
Amigo, tequila, muchacho!

432
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:34,900
The tacos should be arriving any minute now!

433
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:37,200
Taco delivery, right on time!

434
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:39,140
It's arrived!

435
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,980
Damn it!
Even after delivering, I can't stop!

436
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:49,440
Don't do anything reckless!

437
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:52,320
Don't do anything reckless, snap out of it!

438
00:22:56,660 --> 00:22:57,460
Brother!

439
00:22:57,460 --> 00:22:59,260
You came to?

440
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:01,560
Did you save me?

441
00:23:02,060 --> 00:23:03,880
You were trying to make Brother fail.

442
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,000
Even me...

443
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:07,620
We're the only two brothers we've got,
aren't we?

444
00:23:08,980 --> 00:23:09,700
Brother...

445
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,680
Sorry, Brother.

446
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:13,380
Truthfully, Brother, I've always...

447
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:18,360
Seeing my brother find his
own path and charge forward

448
00:23:18,940 --> 00:23:21,640
I actually loved tacos too.

449
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:23,000
I knew.

450
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:25,700
We're twins, after all.

451
00:23:25,700 --> 00:23:30,340
Yet I ended up forcing the Takota
family tradition on you alone.

452
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:33,380
I think I'm the one who should apologize.

453
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:34,940
Brother.

454
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:38,460
Tacos and takoyaki are both foods with
"tako" in their names.

455
00:23:38,460 --> 00:23:41,460
From now on, let's spread them together.

456
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:49,500
We did it! The H2 rocket has
finally launched successfully!

457
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,700
After overcoming repeated failures,
it's finally happening!

458
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:58,020
Hey! It's not my fault!

459
00:23:58,020 --> 00:23:59,040
Nooo!

460
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:30,900
With a bucket in one hand, looking all cool,

461
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:33,620
beef bowl, extra sauce, cloudy broth.

462
00:24:33,620 --> 00:24:36,960
All the frustration of endless overtime

463
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:40,600
melts away in a rush of irritation.

464
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:46,720
Every day's a no-problem blend.

465
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:50,380
After passing through a hot shower,

466
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:53,380
every day's a no-problem blend.

467
00:24:53,380 --> 00:24:56,940
A sleep pillow restores my energy.

468
00:25:00,260 --> 00:25:06,580
Every day's no program.
I love this me just as I am.

469
00:25:06,580 --> 00:25:13,380
Every day's no program.
Monday, with hearts flying everywhere.

470
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:17,420
Every day's no program.

471
00:25:20,460 --> 00:25:25,300
What's so strange about me delivering
newspapers when I was a kid?

472
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:29,640
Sure, getting up early and trudging
around on foot isn't really my style,

473
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:33,560
but I had an unforgettable memory
with my best friend back then.

474
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:38,240
Next time, catch The Newspaper Boy Kakkichi's story,
see you then!

